Subject: Use Boost.Test's portable execution monitor with Fil-C
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Boost.Test initializes its signal monitor before parsing runtime options.
Fil-C rejects fault-signal handlers and alternate signal stacks. Select the
portable monitor locally, keeping all tests, assertions and C++ exception
handling. A Fil-C trap remains a failing process exit, not a recovered signal.

--- a/testsuite/TestSuiteMain.cpp
+++ b/testsuite/TestSuiteMain.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,13 @@
 * OF THIS SOFTWARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGE.
 \**************************************************************************/
 
+#include <boost/config.hpp>
+#ifdef __FILC__
+// Fil-C owns fault handling and does not support alternate signal stacks.
+// Use Boost.Test's portable execution monitor: a runtime trap still fails
+// the process, while ordinary test assertions and exceptions stay enabled.
+#undef BOOST_HAS_SIGACTION
+#endif
 #define BOOST_TEST_MODULE CoinTests
 #define BOOST_TEST_NO_MAIN
 #define BOOST_TEST_ALTERNATIVE_INIT_API
